<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  arm: 6-axis desktop arm - base yaw, shoulder pitch (20:1 cycloidal drive), elbow pitch (GT2 belt),
  FOREARM ROLL (GT2 belt in the elbow block, cad/assemblies/forearm_roll_drive.py), wrist pitch (GT2
  belt) and the NEMA17-pancake wrist roll - + MG996R parallel gripper. Five joints are driven by
  NEMA 17 + MKS SERVO42D kits: the base_yaw / elbow_pitch / wrist_pitch motors are NEMA 17s on the
  pads the links carry (cad/lib/mounts.py: the 48 mm nema17_48mm#1 under the base, nema17_40mm#2..3 on
  the links, + mks_servo42d#1..3, in base_link / upper_arm_link / forearm_link), the shoulder_pitch one
  the cycloidal drive's own 48 mm motor + board, the forearm_roll one the roll drive's own 40 mm motor
  + board (in elbow_link); which CAN id (software/control/src/config.py J1..J3 - three of the five) drives which joint is
  unconfirmed.

  SOURCE OF TRUTH: this file. Every number is derived from the CAD by cad/tools/robot/derive.py
  (cad/robot/frames.py = link partition + joint frames; cad/reference/placements.json = the
  SolidWorks capture) and verified with `./cadtool python tools/robot/derive.py`, check mode
  (tests/test_robot.py runs it). Regenerate meshes with cad/tools/robot/export_link_meshes.py.

  FRAMES (REP-103): base_link on the base's bottom face at the base_yaw axis, Z up, X forward
  (the direction the arm extends). Every joint frame has Z on the joint axis and X along the
  child link's long direction at the capture pose. A child link's frame IS its joint frame at
  the SolidWorks capture pose: ALL JOINTS ARE 0 AT THE CAPTURE POSE and every mesh origin is
  identity. In that pose shoulder_link is yawed +3.694 deg about base_yaw relative to base X (a
  captured pose, not a design offset); the shoulder_pitch, elbow_pitch and wrist_pitch axes are
  parallel (210.0 mm apart each in the pitch plane, with 10 mm and 42 mm offsets along the axis).
  forearm_roll's Z runs along the forearm (elbow -> wrist_pitch, the pitch plane's in-plane direction)
  through the WRIST CENTRE - where the wrist_pitch and wrist_roll axes meet, 17 mm back along the pitch
  axis from the wrist_pitch origin - so the last three axes are concurrent (a spherical wrist); its X is
  the pitch-axis direction (its child's long direction IS the axis). elbow_link is the elbow's driven
  side (the 90T pulley + coupler carrying the roll drive's stator), forearm_link the roll drive's rotor
  (the hollow shaft) + the forearm.

  UNITS: metres, kilograms, radians. MESHES: meshes/<link>.stl in millimetres (scale 0.001),
  one per link in the link frame (visual and collision reuse them; simplified collision
  primitives are a TODO). INERTIALS: OCP BRepGProp on the CAD solids, printed parts at PETG
  1.27 g/cm3, purchased parts at their datasheet/estimated mass (cad/lib/params.py).

  PLACEHOLDERS [ESTIMATE] (cad/lib/params.py): all limits, effort and velocity values; the
  positive-motion sign of every axis (confirm with viewer sweeps); jaw travel range.
  ASSUMPTIONS: j1_coupler (the holder) turns on the base and carries the cycloidal drive's
  stator (housing, motor, gear train) in its yoke - together shoulder_link; the drive's rotor
  (output hub + pins) is bolted to j1_link - together upper_arm_link - so the drive IS the
  shoulder_pitch joint (cad/docs/cycloidal_drive.md, cad/assemblies/cycloidal_drive.py BODIES);
  the GT2 90T pulleys + J3 couplers are bolted to the driven links (elbow_link at elbow_pitch,
  wrist_pitch_link at wrist_pitch); each belt joint's 6806-2RS bearing pair rides with its housing
  (base_link, upper_arm_link, forearm_link; cad/lib/mounts.py), the base_yaw thrust bearing's lower washer and needle
  cage with base_link, its upper washer with j1_coupler (shoulder_link); the MG996R crank linkage is merged into wrist_roll_link;
  jaw_b mirrors jaw_a (mimic, multiplier -1); positive jaw_a = opening.
  UNCONFIRMED: which CAN id (software/control/src/config.py J1..J3) drives which joint - the motors are placed
  (cad/lib/mounts.py) but not mapped; the shoulder_pitch motor is the drive's own NEMA 17 at 20:1
  (cad/lib/params.py CYCLOIDAL_RATIO; software/control/src/config.py still carries gear_ratio 1.0 everywhere). The
  belt motors' masses (280 g) and boards (35 g) are estimates, the wrist_pitch motor's slide position
  (J2_MOTOR_SLIDE_X - what a stock 264-2GT belt sets) too; FOREARM_ROLL_LIMIT_DEG is the hard stop's
  estimate. wrist_roll and the jaws are not driven by software/control/src/config.py, and forearm_roll needs a 4th CAN id.
-->
